  "release_notes": "In the Ready Messages log, only the 'Sender: Ready' body now gets the larger emphasis font on the two most-recent incoming alerts — the '[hh:mm AP]' timestamp prefix stays at the default 10pt across every line so timestamps line up cleanly down the left edge regardless of which line is most-recent or second-most-recent. The size hierarchy on the body is unchanged: the newest incoming Ready is 15pt bold, the previous one is 12pt bold, everything older is plain. The brief background-color flash that plays when a new Ready arrives is now also concentrated on the body for visual consistency with the size emphasis.",
